@echo off
rem asight collector: launch shim for Kimi Code on Windows (RFC 4.8 s6.3), written by the user-path opt-in item of
rem `asight on kimi-code --opt-in kimi-code.cli`. It sets the CA file Node reads (the asight CA, plus any CA you
rem already gave Kimi Code) and this form's kernel listener; an HTTPS_PROXY the shell already set is your choice for
rem that run and is not overridden (that run is not captured). `asight off kimi-code` removes it.
rem The per-pid launch marker (4.6 "mark", the darwin shim's door): a Windows process's environment is never
rem readable from outside (4.8 s10.1), so the tracker confirms this kimi started through the shim by the marker a
rem best-effort background writer records beside the real run - it never touches the run itself, and a marker that
rem does not appear only loses this run's capture. Measured on a Windows test machine: the marker lands ~0.4 s
rem after the kimi.exe child appears, well before its first connection.
if not defined HTTPS_PROXY set "HTTPS_PROXY=__ASIGHT_PROXY__"
set "NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS=__ASIGHT_CA_FILE__"
start "" /b powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File "%~dp0kimi-marker.ps1" -MarkerDir "__ASIGHT_MARKER_DIR__" -Image kimi.exe
"__ASIGHT_REAL_BINARY__" %*
